  "preprocessing": {
    "description": "Section 5 first-order polynomial expansion `(1-p)*pilot^p + p*pilot^(p-1)*U`; the LHS and linear columns use raw U. Pilot: other time-index parity only (`time2`), box moving average, periodic spatial extension and reflected time extension. Window: debiasing_study.py data-driven volume rule, prior 0.01, rounded up to odd and at least 3; no window selection using truth. IB selects 61 x 61 at every tested noise level. Author-code weak supports, state/coordinate scaling and physical coefficient restoration are retained. Both regressions use the same pilot/system and the existing penalty selection. All 100 trials at noise ratios 0, 0.2, 0.5, 0.75, 1 use the original benchmark's observation seeds.",
